	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44493</id><title>I Accuse</title><updated>2026-11-02T18:38:13-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44493" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Saber-Azam_220-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
GENEVA, November 2 (IPS)  - Émile Zola, the well-known French journalist, novelist, playwright, and key figure in theatrical naturalism, who played a significant role in France’s “political liberalization,” inspired me to speak out.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44493&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “I Accuse”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44492</id><title>New Biodiversity Funding Brings Hope for Armenia’s Lake Sevan</title><updated>2026-11-02T09:25:54-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44492" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/IMG_0776.jpeg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/IMG_0776.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/IMG_0776-100x100.jpeg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/IMG_0776.jpeg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
YEREVAN &amp; GEGHARKUNIK PROVINCE, Armenia, November 2 (IPS)  - The midday sun shines brightly over Lake Sevan. In the still waters, a flock of cormorants drifts silently, their black feathers glistening in the autumn light.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44492&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “New Biodiversity Funding Brings Hope for Armenia’s Lake Sevan”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44491</id><title>The Commonwealth Has 2.7 Billion Reasons to Act</title><updated>2026-11-02T07:06:11-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44491" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Shirley-Botchwey.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Shirley-Botchwey.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Shirley-Botchwey-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Shirley-Botchwey.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
LONDON, November 2 (IPS)  - Ours is not a new realisation. The Commonwealth is responding to what world leaders have acknowledged for many years: ‘business as usual’ cannot reverse the unsustainable course the world finds itself, from economic to climate crises and the growing lack of trust in governance institutions, both national and multilateral.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44491&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The Commonwealth Has 2.7 Billion Reasons to Act”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44489</id><title>WFP Warnings Become a Reality as Food Insecurity in Haiti on Track to Reach Record Highs</title><updated>2026-11-02T05:37:39-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44489" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/WFP_HTI_Emily-Pinna.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/WFP_HTI_Emily-Pinna.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/WFP_HTI_Emily-Pinna-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/WFP_HTI_Emily-Pinna.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti, November 2 (IPS)  - Warnings by the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP) that Haiti’s fragile food security gains could quickly unravel are becoming a reality. New analysis indicates acute hunger in the country is continuing its upward trajectory and is set to reach record levels. Violence, economic instability, poor agricultural performance and displacement, along with the growing impact of El Niño, are driving this bleak outlook.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44489&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “WFP Warnings Become a Reality as Food Insecurity in Haiti on Track to Reach Record Highs”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44490</id><title>The UN Human Rights Council at 20: Credibility in Question</title><updated>2026-11-02T05:26:36-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44490" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/A-delegate-casts_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/A-delegate-casts_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/A-delegate-casts_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/A-delegate-casts_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
MONTEVIDEO, Uruguay / BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, November 2 (IPS)  - On 13 October, Burundi won a second consecutive term on the UN Human Rights Council, the UN’s main human rights body. The &lt;a href=&quot;https://monitor.civicus.org/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CIVICUS Monitor&lt;/a&gt; rates civic space in Burundi as &lt;a href=&quot;https://monitor.civicus.org/country/burundi/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;closed&lt;/a&gt;, the worst category. Its government has spent years silencing civil society, critics and opposition parties, including through extrajudicial killings, forced disappearances and torture.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44490&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The UN Human Rights Council at 20: Credibility in Question”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44496</id><title>Ukraine: WFP provides hot meals to Oleshky evacuees as UN pushes to restore power before winter</title><updated>2026-11-02T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44496" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026-UNDP-Nikolaj-Waldau.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026-UNDP-Nikolaj-Waldau.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026-UNDP-Nikolaj-Waldau.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026-UNDP-Nikolaj-Waldau.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN World Food Programme (WFP) is providing emergency food assistance to more than 400 people who were able to leave the Russian-occupied city of Oleshky, in Ukraine’s Kherson region, during a brief local ceasefire. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44496&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ukraine: WFP provides hot meals to Oleshky evacuees as UN pushes to restore power before winter”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44495</id><title>Ethiopia: Violence in the north is pushing health system to the brink, WHO chief warns</title><updated>2026-11-02T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44495" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026_Adobe_Ethiopia.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026_Adobe_Ethiopia.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026_Adobe_Ethiopia.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/02-11-2026_Adobe_Ethiopia.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The head of the World Health Organization (WHO) called on Monday for greater protection for civilians caught in conflict in northern Ethiopia following deadly drone strikes this past weekend.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44495&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ethiopia: Violence in the north is pushing health system to the brink, WHO chief warns”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44494</id><title>Six in seven journalist murders go unpunished,  UNESCO reports</title><updated>2026-11-02T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44494" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/29-10-2026-Adobe-Stock-journalist.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/29-10-2026-Adobe-Stock-journalist.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/29-10-2026-Adobe-Stock-journalist.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/29-10-2026-Adobe-Stock-journalist.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Global impunity for journalist killings has risen for the first time in more than a decade, while the growing use of drones is an emerging threat for reporters in conflict zones, according to the latest report from UN cultural organization UNESCO. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/02/44494&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Six in seven journalist murders go unpunished,  UNESCO reports”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44488</id><title>Breaking the silence in Mexico’s barracks</title><updated>2026-11-01T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44488" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/12-10-26_UN_Human-Rights_Zorayda_Gallegos.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/12-10-26_UN_Human-Rights_Zorayda_Gallegos.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/12-10-26_UN_Human-Rights_Zorayda_Gallegos.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/12-10-26_UN_Human-Rights_Zorayda_Gallegos.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Mexico’s armed forces, an order from a superior is meant to be obeyed without question. For many women in uniform, investigative journalist Zorayda Gallegos found, that can include an order to step into an officer’s bedroom.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44488&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Breaking the silence in Mexico’s barracks”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44487</id><title>COP17: Nations chart ‘Yerevan Pathway’ to speed up action for nature</title><updated>2026-11-01T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44487" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/31-05-2023_Agricultural%20Heritage%20Systems%203.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/31-05-2023_Agricultural%20Heritage%20Systems%203.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/31-05-2023_Agricultural%20Heritage%20Systems%203.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/31-05-2023_Agricultural%20Heritage%20Systems%203.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At the halfway mark to 2030, countries meeting in Armenia have agreed a roadmap to accelerate action for nature, after a global review found the world off track to meet its biodiversity targets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/01/44487&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “COP17: Nations chart ‘Yerevan Pathway’ to speed up action for nature”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0081s ch:0 -->